{"name":"Beach Dune","hex":"#c6bb9c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"},{"term":"dune","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ridge or hill of sand piled up by currents of wind or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dune"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach","wikidata":"Q40080"},{"title":"Dune","blocks":[{"text":"A dune is a landform composed of wind- or water-driven sand. It typically takes the form of a mound, ridge, or hill. An area with dunes is called a dune system or a dune complex. A large dune complex is called a dune field, while broad, flat regions covered with wind-swept sand or dunes, with little or no vegetation, are called ergs or sand seas. Dunes occur in different shapes and sizes, but most kinds of dunes are longer on the stoss (upflow) side, where the sand is pushed up the dune, and have a shorter slip face in the lee side. The valley or trough between dunes is called a dune slack."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg/330px-Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune","wikidata":"Q25391"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/1280px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg/500px-Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg/1280px-Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg/500px-Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMan_o'war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Beach_zones.png/500px-Beach_zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Beach_zones.png/500px-Beach_zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A berm is a nearly horizontal portion that stays dry except during extremely high tides and storms. The swash zone is alternately covered and exposed by wave run-up. The beach face is the sloping section below the berm that is exposed to the swash of the waves. The wrack line (not shown here) is the highest reach of the daily tide where organic and inorganic debris is deposited by wave action. May have sand dunes.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeach_zones.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Summer_versus_winter_beach.png/500px-Summer_versus_winter_beach.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Summer_versus_winter_beach.png/500px-Summer_versus_winter_beach.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The differences between summer and winter on beaches in areas where the winter conditions are rougher and waves have a shorter wavelength but higher energy. In winter, sand from the beach is stored offshore.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASummer_versus_winter_beach.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg/500px-Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg/1280px-Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg/500px-Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3